 ("Main idea", "The passage is mainly about:", ["a student who turns a failed project into a lesson and is recognized for her thinking", "a brother and sister who build a volcano together", "a science teacher who judges a fair", "how to build a model volcano"], "Priya studies why the volcano failed, presents that, and wins a ribbon for scientific thinking."),
 ("Details", "Priya concludes that her volcano collapsed because:", ["the last coat of paste was too wet and the layers underneath never dried", "her brother knocked it over", "she used too much baking soda", "the chicken wire was too thin"], "Paragraph 3 gives her conclusion."),
 ("Figurative language", "The comparison of the exposed chamber to \"a broken bone\" mainly emphasizes:", ["how badly damaged the volcano looked", "that Priya had been injured", "the volcano's bright colors", "how strong the chicken wire was"], "A broken bone showing through suggests serious, visible damage."),
 ("Theme", "Which statement best expresses a theme of the passage?", ["Learning from failure can be as valuable as success.", "Winning first place is all that matters.", "Older siblings always give good advice.", "Science projects should be finished early."], "Mr. Ochoa's idea and the ribbon both show that learning from failure matters."),
