 ("Main idea", "The passage is mainly about:", ["a community's quilting tradition and its recognition as art", "how to make a quilt", "the geography of the Alabama River", "the history of the Whitney Museum"], "It describes the tradition, the design, museum recognition, and questions it raised."),
 ("Details", "According to the passage, the quilters often used materials such as:", ["worn work clothes and feed sacks", "new fabric bought in cities", "silk from overseas", "paper and paint"], "Paragraph 1 lists them."),
 ("Vocabulary in context", "As used in the passage, \"improvised\" most nearly means:", ["created freely without following a fixed plan", "copied exactly", "repaired", "sold"], "The quilters didn't follow patterns exactly; designs shifted as they worked."),
 ("Structure", "The last paragraph mainly serves to:", ["raise questions about art and fairness prompted by the quilts' fame", "describe how the quilts are sewn", "list the museums that showed the quilts", "explain why the quilters stopped working"], "It presents the open questions the quilters have discussed."),
