 ("Main idea", "The passage is mainly about:", ["a girl who uses her uncle's advice to find her way back to shore in thick fog", "a girl who learns to kayak for the first time", "an uncle who is angry at his niece", "a boat race in the fog"], "Elena listens for sounds, as her uncle taught her, and returns safely."),
 ("Reasoning", "Elena decides the beach is \"ahead and slightly right\" because:", ["she knows the bell buoy is north of the beach and hears it on her left", "she can see her uncle's truck", "the wind is blowing toward shore", "the tide is coming in"], "Paragraph 3 explains her reasoning from the bell."),
 ("Inferences", "The detail that her uncle's voice was \"cracking in a way she had never heard before\" suggests that he was:", ["very frightened for her", "angry at her", "losing his voice from a cold", "laughing at her"], "A cracking voice he'd never had before shows fear and emotion."),
 ("Character", "The uncle's actions at the end of the passage mainly suggest that he:", ["is relieved and deeply cares about Elena", "plans to punish Elena", "is indifferent to what happened", "wants to go kayaking himself"], "He says nothing about the danger and holds on \"a little longer\": relief and care."),
